  triage:title "Three near-duplicate connection-admission strategies" ;
  triage:description "ConnectionWorkerPool (local_ipc_transport/connection_workers.rs:35-135), DispatchWorkerPool (local_ipc_transport/request_worker.rs:50-160), and spawn_windows_connection (local_tcp_transport.rs:433-470) implement overlapping worker-pool and connection-admission logic with the same pattern: fixed admission queue, N worker threads pulling from bounded sync_channel, panic recovery, and shutdown handling. Arch-ctm confirmed (2026-08-03T02:09:03Z) this is real duplication and load-bearing (distinct purpose per transport), but deferred to separate local-HTTP admission-consolidation refactor, NOT in scope for current branch fix/localipcwake-accept-interrupt. Recommended scope: track separately as 'local-HTTP connection-pool factory' cleanup (no branch/sprint assigned yet)." ;
